# Process Controller Consolidation Implementation Plan

## Goal

Make Converge the sole top-level controller for this OpenCode workflow and for any review/orchestration flow in which Converge is selected. TDD, systematic debugging, and completion verification become bounded Executor-local methods. Preserve the evidence-calibrated `8/3/3` stock quality-loop ceiling, use the existing task envelope for optional task-level cost control, and upstream only demonstrated cross-project defects in `init-agent-docs` without making generated projects depend on Converge.

## Authoritative Inputs

- Repositories:
  - `C:\Users\Administrator\Documents\Github\converge-skill`
  - `C:\Users\Administrator\Documents\Github\init-agent-docs`
- At initial planning time both repositories were clean and `0 0` ahead/behind their configured upstream branches after `git fetch`; the branches were `master` and `main` respectively. At this repair, both worktrees contain the reviewed but uncommitted D1/D2/D4-D6 implementation. Those edits are protected input: preserve them, do not reset or overwrite them, and implement only the eventual corrective delta.
- Converge governance changes require ultraverge before implementation: at least three independent initial reviewers, convergence of all blocking findings, and a mandatory post-convergence design review.
- The three ultraverge initial reviews disagreed on `需重新设计` versus `阻断需修复`; the credible conceptual minority finding upgrades this plan to full convergence.
- While this repair is authored, only this active `plan.md` and append-only `attempts.md` may change. No implementation file may be changed, and nothing may be committed or pushed.

